From: Sam Attard <sattard@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:10:09 +0000
Subject: tls: adapt the upstream SPKI blocklist for Electron

Node.js v24.22.1 ships the SubjectPublicKeyInfo blocklist that Electron
previously carried in this patch (same compiled-in entries, applied to
every SSL_CTX via InstallCertVerifyCallback). What remains here is what
Electron still needs on top of it:

- BoringSSL's sk_X509_num() returns size_t, so the new CheckSPKIs() loop
  uses OPENSSL_SIZE_T to build cleanly with -Wsign-compare.
- Upstream only exposes the test-only list extension through
  internalBinding('crypto'). Export C++ hooks that share the same list
  and mutex so Electron's testing binding can extend it at runtime.
- Add entries that are not yet in the upstream list, mirroring the ones
  Electron adds to Chromium's net blocklist.

